// NOOPSigning.xcconfig — per-Mac signing for Xcode builds of the iPhone app, its widgets and the watch app.
//
// Attached to the NOOPiOS, NOOPiOSWidgets, NOOPWatch and NOOPWatchComplications targets (project.yml,
// configFiles). On its own it sets nothing, so the project.yml defaults apply and neither the CI compile
// check nor the TestFlight build (fastlane build_noop, which writes your team into a temporary copy of
// project.yml) is affected.
//
// To build and run on your iPhone from Xcode, run `Tools/setup-xcode.sh <TEAMID>` once. It writes
// Config/Local.xcconfig (git-ignored, never committed) with your Team ID and the same identifiers the
// TestFlight build uses (com.<TEAMID>.noopapp.noop…), so both ways install the same app, unless NOOP_APP_ID
// pins the id of a NOOP already on the iPhone (an AltStore/SideStore install), so Xcode updates that one and
// its data stays. A target-level xcconfig outranks the project-level NOOP_BUNDLE_PREFIX / NOOP_APP_ID /
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM defaults in project.yml.

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
